+## Platform contract
 
-## Structure
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Input (adapter view) | features (+ labels in research mode) |
+| Output (`WTDataSchema`) | prediction + probability |
+| Record format | `wt-pm.platform.v1` |
+| Typical latency | 800 ms |
+| Deployment targets | cloud, edge_cpu |
+| Resource requirements | xgboost, scikit-learn |
+| Fallback | `m10-random-forest` |
+| Subsystem focus | whole turbine |
+| Hermes tool | `diagnose / explain` |
+
+Records follow the shared `WTDataSchema` (`wt-pm.platform.v1`): `timestamp`, `turbine_id` and `model_id` are required; every other field is optional, so a model fills in only what it honestly produces and the fusion layer can tell absence from a zero.
+
+## Platform layers
+
+| Layer | What this model does there |
+|---|---|
+| **Fusion** | Primary tabular vote in the fault-classification ensemble |
+| **XAI** | Primary TreeExplainer subject - the explain tool's default |
+| **Edge** | Distilled into the m25 relay and quantized by m24 |
+| **Fallback** | Receives fallbacks from m01 and m12 when their feature views are unavailable |
+
+Layers are described once, in the catalog, and referenced by every model that participates in them: fusion, calibrated uncertainty, drift and data trust, explainability, physics constraints, the safety gate, the evaluation protocol and the Hermes agent.
+
+## How it connects to the other 24
+
+**Receives from**
+
+- **13. LSTM SCADA Anomaly (reference contract hub)** (`m05-lstm-scada-anomaly`) - anomaly records for fault triage
+
+**Feeds**
+
+- **22. TinyML ESP32 Safety Relay** (`m25-tinyml-safety`) - distilled depth-5 tree exported to the ESP32 relay
+- **24. XAI SHAP Interpretable** (`m21-xai-shap`) - SHAP explanations of boosted-tree alerts
+
+Related pages: [13 LSTM SCADA](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly), [22 TinyML Safety](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-tinyml-esp32-safety-relay), [24 XAI SHAP](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-xai-shap-interpretable)
